============================================================
II. SKILLS & PERKS
============================================================
One-Handed (Adept)
He fights with a woodcutter's axe, using the choppy, brutal swings of a man
used to felling trees.
  Fighting Stance: Can make an extra attack as a Minor Action for 3 FP.
  Hack and Slash: Attacks inflict Bleeding (1 damage/turn) on a successful
    hit.

Heavy Armor (Apprentice)
He doesn't wear plate, but his skin has hardened into a callous-like hide
from the constant cycle of burning and healing.
  Juggernaut: Grants intrinsic DR bonuses as if wearing armor.

Restoration (Innate/Corrupted)
He cannot cast healing spells, but his body naturally channels blood magic
to fuel his mutation.
  Avoid Death: Once per adventure, if reduced to 0 HP, he immediately heals
    for 10 HP. Note: this is different from the Restoration spell version.
    A death-blow of more than 10 excess damage would still down him.

============================================================
III. SPECIAL ABILITIES & TRAITS
============================================================
Unique Mechanic: The Overcharge Engine
Hirt does not function like a normal living being. He is a furnace.

1. Hyper-Metabolism (The Burn): Hirt loses energy violently. He must feed
   twice as often as a normal vampire (every 12 hours). If he fails to
   feed, he enters Critical Burn:
     Effect: Disadvantage on all rolls. Takes 1 Irreducible Damage every
     10 minutes.

2. The Sanguine Battery: Hirt does not heal normally from feeding. When he
   uses Bio-Siphon or bites a target, the healing he receives is converted
   into Temporary HP.
     Uncapped: There is NO LIMIT to his Temporary HP. He can stack health
     indefinitely during a fight.
     Decay: He loses 5 Temporary HP per 10 minutes out of combat as his
     body consumes itself.
     Note: he cannot truly heal by any means other than rest. When Hirt
     rests, his Temp HP is converted into true HP; the excess is vented
     as heat.

3. Burning: his blood is boiling hot. He takes half damage from sources of
   fire and is immune to frost effects.

Combat Abilities

Bio-Siphon (Major Action -- 10 FP)
  Range: 30ft.
  Effect: Hirt screams as he vents the reactor, firing a raw, jagged beam
    of red energy from his chest/hands.
  Roll: Magic.
  Damage: 5 Irreducible Damage and 5 Fire damage.
  Benefit: Hirt gains 20 Temporary HP.

Mist Form (Unstable) (Reaction -- 8 FP)
  Trigger: When hit by a physical attack.
  Effect: Hirt dissolves into a cloud of boiling red steam. He is Immune
    to Physical Damage until the start of his next turn.
  Hazard: Any creature standing in the mist (adjacent to him) takes 4 Fire
    Damage (his blood is boiling hot).

Sanguine Overload (Passive)
  Trigger: When Hirt has 84+ Total HP including Temporary HP.
  Effect: His blood runs so hot it heats his weapon. His melee attacks
    deal an additional +2 Fire Damage.

The Failed Serum (Daywalker)
  Effect: Hirt takes 0 Damage from Sunlight. He appears human, if sickly.
    This was Valerius's only success.
  The Cost: He gains NO standard Vampire attribute bonuses (Strength/
    Speed/Charm). He is just a man in pain.

